WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.300
One small line in Avengers: Infinity War could
hold the key to understanding that shocking

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.300
ending.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.590
And it's also a cool callback to 2016's standalone
Doctor Strange flick.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.640
Warning: Major Infinity War spoilers ahead!

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.570
Doctor Strange's claim that he sees only one
of "14 million six hundred and five" possible

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.429
future scenarios in which the Avengers defeat
Thanos could help to explain some of his,

00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:26.300
well, strange behavior in the movie's second
half.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.259
Infinity War features the MCU's most powerful
heroes fighting to stop Thanos from attaining

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:35.100
five Infinity stones and wiping out half the
life in the universe.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.890
However, their plan is thrown for a loop when
Doctor Strange gives Thanos the Time Stone

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.019
in exchange for him sparing Tony Stark's life.

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:47.370
The move appears to have been a fatal one
for Strange, who is wiped out after Thanos

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.929
gets the Mind Stone and carries out his plot.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:55.059
But before he turns to dust, Strange tells
Stark that "there was no other way," which

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:58.769
suggests that giving up the stone is critical
to the Avengers' victory.

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:00.030
This could mean a few things.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.499
It could suggest that Stark will have a key
part to play in defeating Thanos, and had

00:01:03.499 --> 00:01:04.650
to be spared.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:09.100
It could also mean that Thanos wiping out
half the life in the universe temporarily

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:14.140
is actually part of Strange's winning scenario,
which brings us to that subtle callback.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.159
In the character's standalone film, Strange's
mentor the Ancient One tells him she can never

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:20.760
see past her own demise.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.870
"I've spent so many years peering through
time, looking at this exact moment.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.630
But I can't see past it."

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.700
She then adds:

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:36.619
"I've prevented countless terrible futures
and after each one there's always another,

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:40.090
and they all lead here but never further."

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:44.780
So if Doctor Strange is able to see beyond
the moment when he is apparently dusted by

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:49.740
Thanos, it means he didn't really expire,
and Thanos' handiwork won't last in the scenario

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.350
in which the Avengers win.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.190
This supports the theory that the Avengers
are just stuck in the Soul World - a dimension

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:59.700
inside the Soul Stone where dead characters
sometimes go in the comics - and can be brought

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.670
back to life for Avengers 4.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:05.719
It'll be awhile before we know for sure what's
up with the doc's enigmatic words, with Avengers

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:09.090
4 not slated to hit theaters until May 3rd,
2019.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:13.200
But for now, he's definitely given Marvel
fans something strange - and hopeful - to

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.200
think about.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.200
Thanks for watching!

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.659
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

